      "bg": "--color-bg-surface",
      "layer": "semantic"
    },
    {
      "$comment": "Subtle ink on the CANVAS, which is the half that was missing. Only the surface pairing was declared, and the two are not the same measurement once the canvas is tinted away from the surface: in light this reads 5.29:1 where the surface reads 6.13, and at the previous #64748b it was 4.20 against a canvas the surface pairing still passed at 4.76. Every consumer that sits on the page rather than in a card — the DataView toolbar's result count, a section's lead line — failed axe while the declared pairing stayed green, which is exactly the coverage claim this file exists to make honest.",
      "id": "subtle-on-canvas",
      "label": "subtle text on the canvas",
      "fg": "--color-fg-subtle",
      "bg": "--color-bg-canvas",
      "layer": "semantic"
    },
    {
      "id": "body-on-subtle",
